---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<Article
  title="Terms of Use"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="Terms governing use of the Marshall Sheds website."
  lede="These terms cover your use of this website. Terms of sale are separate and are provided with your quote and order documents."
  crumbs={[]}
>
  <div class="admin-note">
    <strong>Publish note — remove before launch.</strong> This is a starting template, not
    legal advice. Have it reviewed by a lawyer, and make sure it does not conflict with your
    dealer agreement — particularly anything about how you describe the manufacturer
    relationship, warranty, or use of manufacturer trademarks.
  </div>

  <h2>About this site</h2>
  <p>
    This website is operated by Marshall Sheds, an authorized independent dealer of
    pre-engineered steel buildings. We are not the manufacturer. Buildings are produced by our
    manufacturing partner and shipped direct from their production facilities.
  </p>

  <h2>Information on this site</h2>
  <p>
    Product information, dimensions, specifications and guidance on this site are provided for
    general reference. Specifications, availability and pricing can change, and the
    engineering that applies to your building is determined by your specific site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is an offer to sell at a stated price. A binding price and
    specification comes only from a written quote issued to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Guidance is not engineering advice</h2>
  <p>
    Our guides cover general principles — foundations, ventilation, code processes and so on.
    They are not a substitute for engineering, and they are not a substitute for your local
    building department. Requirements vary by jurisdiction and by site, and only your stamped
    drawings and your building department can tell you what applies to your project.
  </p>

  <h2>Quotes and orders</h2>
  <p>
    Quotes are valid for the period stated on them. Steel is a commodity and pricing moves.
    Terms of sale — including deposit, payment, lead time, delivery, cancellation and warranty
    — are set out in your quote and order documents, and those documents govern the
    transaction rather than this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Providing accurate site information, including the exact delivery address</li>
    <li>Obtaining permits and approvals for your project</li>
    <li>Site preparation, foundation design and construction</li>
    <li>Offloading the delivery</li>
    <li>Assembly in accordance with the instructions and stamped drawings</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site, including text and design, belongs to Marshall Sheds or is used with
    permission. Trademarks belonging to our manufacturing partner and other third parties
    remain the property of their respective owners.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses
    arising from use of this website. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by
    law, and nothing here affects the warranty provided with your building.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. Continued use of the site means you accept the current version.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to
    {!site.emailPending && <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.info}`}>{site.emails.info}</a>}
    {!site.emailPending && ' or raised through the '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Article>

<style>
  .admin-note {
    padding: 1rem 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #dc2626 8%, transparent);
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, #dc2626 45%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .admin-note strong { display: block; color: #dc2626; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
</style>
